1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Test 4. This is the IELTS listening test.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
You will hear a number of different recordings and you will have to answer questions on what you hear.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,000
There will be time for you to read the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
All the recordings will be played once only.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The test is in four parts.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
At the end of the test you will be given ten minutes to transfer your answers to the answer sheet.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Now turn to part one.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Part one.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
You will hear a man phoning to inquire about a cleaning service for his apartment.

10
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
First you have some time to look at questions one to five.

11
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Part two.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Now listen carefully and answer questions one to five.

13
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Hello. Easy life cleaning services. Jacinta speaking.

14
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Oh hello. I'm looking for a cleaning service for my apartment. Do you do domestic cleaning?

15
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Sure.

16
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Well it's just a one bedroom flat. Do you have a basic cleaning package?

17
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Yes. For a one bedroom flat we're probably looking at about two hours for a clean.

18
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
So we do a thorough clean of all surfaces in each room and polish them where necessary.

19
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Does your apartment have carpets?

20
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:55,000
No I don't have any but the floor would need cleaning.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Of course. We do that in every room and we do a thorough clean of the kitchen and bathroom.

22
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Okay.

23
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Then we have some additional services which you can request if you want.

24
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
So for example we can clean your oven for you every week.

25
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Actually I hardly ever use that but can you do the fridge?

26
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Sure. Would you like that done every week?

27
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Yes definitely. And would ironing clothes be an additional service you can do?

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Yes of course.

29
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
It wouldn't be much just my shirts for work that week.

30
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:32,000
That's fine and we could also clean your microwave if you want.

31
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:36,000
No I wipe that out pretty regularly so there's no need for that.

32
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
We also offer additional services that you might want a bit less often say every month.

33
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
So for example if the inside of your windows need cleaning we could do that.

34
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:54,000
Yes that'd be good. I'm on the 15th floor so the outside gets done regularly by specialists

35
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
but the inside does get a bit grubby.

36
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
And we could arrange for your curtains to get cleaned if necessary.

37
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:05,000
No they're okay but would you be able to do something about the balcony?

38
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:11,000
It's quite small and I don't use it much but it could do with a wash every month or so.

39
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Yes we can get the pressure washer onto that.

40
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Before you hear the rest of the conversation you have some time to look at questions 6 to 10.

41
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Now listen and answer questions 6 to 10.

42
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Now if you're interested we do offer some other possibilities to do with general maintenance.

43
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:06,000
For example if you have a problem with water and you need a plumber in a hurry

44
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
we can put you in touch with a reliable one who can come out straight away.

45
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
And the same thing if you need an electrician.

46
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Right that's good to know. I've only just moved here so I don't have any of those sorts of contacts.

47
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:27,000
And I don't know if this is of interest to you but we also offer a special vacuum cleaning system

48
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:34,000
which can improve the indoor air quality of your home by capturing up to 99% of all the dust in the air.

49
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:38,000
So if you're troubled by allergies this can make a big difference.

50
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Right in fact I don't have that sort of problem but I'll bear it in mind.

51
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Now can you tell me a bit about your cleaning staff?

52
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Of course. So all our cleaners are very carefully selected.

53
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:55,000
When they apply to us they have to undergo a security check with the police

54
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:59,000
to make sure they don't have any sort of criminal background.

55
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:02,000
And of course they have to provide references as well.

56
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Then if we think they might be suitable for the job we give them training for it.

57
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,000
That lasts for two weeks so it's very thorough and at the end of it they have a test.

58
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,000
If they pass that we take them on but we monitor them very carefully.

59
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:22,000
We ask all our clients to complete a review of their performance after every visit

60
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:27,000
and to email it to us so we can pick up any problems straight away and deal with them.

61
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Okay well that all sounds good.

62
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:33,000
And will I always have the same cleaner?

63
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Yes we do our best to organise it that way and we usually manage it.

64
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Good that's fine.

65
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Right so I'd like to go ahead and...

66
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
That is the end of part one.

67
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:52,000
You now have half a minute to check your answers to part one.

68
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Thank you.

